          },
          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>Which RMNCH mortality indicator is most sensitive to the quality of care during </p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>Which RMNCH mortality indicator is most sensitive to the quality of care during labour and delivery?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Maternal Mortality Ratio</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>MMR captures maternal deaths up to 42 days after delivery, so it reflects overall obstetric care quality rather than intrapartum care specifically.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Infant Mortality Rate</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>IMR covers the entire first year of life. Its sensitivity to intrapartum care is diluted by post-neonatal causes such as infections and malnutrition.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Perinatal Mortality Rate</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. PMR combines stillbirths after 28 weeks with deaths in the first 7 days — both outcomes directly influenced by intrapartum events such as birth asphyxia and cord complications.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Under-5 Mortality Rate</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>U5MR extends to age five, so it is heavily influenced by infectious diseases and nutritional deficiencies beyond the newborn period.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The Perinatal Mortality Rate (stillbirths ≥28 weeks + first-week deaths, per 1,000 total births) focuses on the narrow window around delivery, making it the most sensitive indicator of intrapartum care quality."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Well done. The Perinatal Mortality Rate uniquely captures events around the time of delivery, making it the best proxy for intrapartum care quality."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
