          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>In the three delays framework for maternal mortality, which delay do schemes suc</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>In the three delays framework for maternal mortality, which delay do schemes such as Janani Suraksha Yojana (JSY) and Janani Shishu Suraksha Karyakram (JSSK) primarily address?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Delay in recognising the complication</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Recognition delay is addressed through community awareness and ASHA surveillance, not through financial incentive schemes.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Delay in deciding to seek care</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. JSY provides cash incentives for institutional delivery and JSSK ensures free treatment and transport, removing the financial and social barriers that cause families to delay the decision to seek care.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Delay in reaching the health facility</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Transport delay is addressed by systems like the 108 ambulance network and strategically placed delivery points, not by financial schemes.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Delay in receiving treatment at the facility</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Delay in receiving treatment relates to facility preparedness and staffing. JSY and JSSK work on the demand side — removing barriers before the woman reaches the facility.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "JSY and JSSK address the second delay — the decision to seek care. By providing cash incentives (JSY) and cashless services (JSSK), they remove the financial and social barriers that cause families to hesitate before seeking emergency obstetric care."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct. By removing financial barriers, JSY and JSSK target the second delay — the decision to seek care — which is often the most socially complex of the three."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
