          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>A pregnant woman identified as high-risk at her booking visit misses her schedul</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A pregnant woman identified as high-risk at her booking visit misses her scheduled 28-week antenatal appointment. Which component of the RMNCH+A tracking system is designed to detect this individual missed visit?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>HMIS indicators</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>HMIS indicators aggregate population-level data such as the percentage of women completing four or more ANC visits. They monitor district-level trends, not individual missed appointments.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Maternal Death Surveillance and Response</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>MDSR is activated retrospectively after a maternal death to identify where the delay occurred. It does not prospectively track missed visits.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Mother and Child Protection Card</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. The MCP Card, given at the first antenatal visit, records the visit schedule, risk status, and immunisation history. When a community health worker reviews it and finds a missed 28-week visit, she flags the woman to the medical officer.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Village Health, Sanitation and Nutrition Committee</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>VHSNCs meet monthly to discuss community health issues and maintain accountability, but they are not designed to track individual patients' appointment schedules.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The Mother and Child Protection Card is the answer. It travels with the woman and records her visit schedule and risk status, enabling the community health worker to spot a missed visit and flag her to the medical officer for follow-up."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Well done. The Mother and Child Protection Card is the individual-level tracking tool that links community detection to facility care, ensuring no high-risk woman falls through the gaps."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
